{
  "path": "lua/common/kdtreepoint3d.lua",
  "module": "K-d tree for 3D points. Offers two kinds of queries: the points in a box (query / queryNotNested, iterators) and the nearest point to a given point (findNearest). Typical for finding the road node or object nearest to a position. Flow: new -> preLoad -> build -> queries.",
  "usage": "local kdTreeP3d = require('kdtreepoint3d')\nlocal kdT = kdTreeP3d.new(itemCount)\nfor id, p in pairs(points) do kdT:preLoad(id, p.x, p.y, p.z) end\nkdT:build()\nlocal nearestId, dist = kdT:findNearest(x, y, z)\nfor id in kdT:queryNotNested(xmin, ymin, zmin, xmax, ymax, zmax) do ... end",
  "notes": [
    "Each point occupies 4 values in self.items (x, y, z, id); before build() itemCount counts values, after build() it is the number of points.",
    "The usage comment writes `kdT:preload` but the actual method is preLoad (capital L).",
    "findNearest returns the id and the DISTANCE (square root, not the squared value). It uses self.qPoint and self.stack: not reentrant, and it does not work before build. It uses the global square (mathlib).",
    "queryNotNested cannot be nested (state reused); query can. Query bounds clamped to ±1.7e308.",
    "No clear() method in this version (unlike kdtreebox2d)."
  ],
  "fields": {},
